<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>{{ report_title }} - Penetration Test Report</title>
<style>
  /* === Base Styles === */
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: #2c3e50;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background: #f8f9fa;
  }
  .container {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: white;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
  }

  /* === Cover Page === */
  .cover {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 80px 0 60px;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #2c3e50;
    margin-bottom: 50px;
  }
  .cover h1 {
    font-size: 36px;
    color: #2c3e50;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    letter-spacing: -1px;
  }
  .cover .subtitle {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #7f8c8d;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .cover .meta {
    display: inline-block;
    text-align: left;
    background: #ecf0f1;
    padding: 20px 30px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .cover .meta div { margin: 4px 0; }
  .cover .meta strong { color: #2c3e50; display: inline-block; min-width: 120px; }

  /* === Section Headers === */
  h2 {
    color: #2c3e50;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-size: 22px;
  }
  h3 {
    color: #34495e;
    font-size: 18px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  /* === Summary Table === */
  .summary-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 15px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .summary-card {
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-align: center;
    color: white;
  }
  .summary-card .count { font-size: 32px; font-weight: bold; }
  .summary-card .label { font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; }
  .critical { background: #c0392b; }
  .high { background: #e74c3c; }
  .medium { background: #f39c12; }
  .low { background: #27ae60; }

  /* === Findings === */
  .finding {
    border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
    border-left: 5px solid #e74c3c;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 25px 30px;
    margin: 25px 0;
    background: #fafafa;
  }
  .finding.critical-finding { border-left-color: #c0392b; }
  .finding.high-finding { border-left-color: #e74c3c; }
  .finding.medium-finding { border-left-color: #f39c12; }
  .finding.low-finding { border-left-color: #27ae60; }

  .finding-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .finding-title { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: #2c3e50; margin: 0; }

  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: white;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }
  .badge-critical { background: #c0392b; }
  .badge-high { background: #e74c3c; }
  .badge-medium { background: #f39c12; }
  .badge-low { background: #27ae60; }
  .cvss { background: #34495e; color: white; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; }

  .finding-meta {
    background: white;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin: 12px 0;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .finding-meta strong { color: #2c3e50; display: inline-block; min-width: 90px; }

  code, pre {
    background: #2c3e50;
    color: #ecf0f1;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  pre { padding: 12px 16px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }

  .section-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #2c3e50;
    margin-top: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    font-size: 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }

  /* === Footer === */
  .footer {
    margin-top: 60px;
    padding-top: 25px;
    border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
    text-align: center;
    color: #95a5a6;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  /* === Print Styles === */
  @media print {
    body { background: white; }
    .container { box-shadow: none; padding: 20px; }
    .finding { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">

  <!-- === COVER PAGE === -->
  <div class="cover">
    <h1>{{ report_title }}</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">Web Application Penetration Test Report</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <div><strong>Target:</strong> {{ target }}</div>
      <div><strong>Test Date:</strong> {{ test_date }}</div>
      <div><strong>Tester:</strong> {{ tester_name }}</div>
      <div><strong>Report Type:</strong> Automated Vulnerability Assessment</div>
      <div><strong>Total Findings:</strong> {{ total_findings }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- === EXECUTIVE SUMMARY === -->
  <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
  <p>
    This report presents the findings of an automated security assessment conducted against
    <strong>{{ target }}</strong> on {{ test_date }}. The assessment was performed using a custom-built
    Python vulnerability scanner that systematically identifies common web application security weaknesses.
  </p>
  <p>
    A total of <strong>{{ total_findings }} vulnerabilities</strong> were identified across
    {{ vuln_class_count }} distinct vulnerability classes. All findings are categorized as
    <strong>High severity</strong> and represent significant risks that should be remediated promptly.
  </p>
  <p>
    The identified vulnerabilities could allow an attacker to compromise user data, hijack user sessions,
    or gain unauthorized access to sensitive information. Detailed technical findings, proof-of-concept
    payloads, and remediation guidance are provided in subsequent sections.
  </p>

  <!-- === FINDINGS SUMMARY GRID === -->
  <h2>Findings Summary</h2>
  <div class="summary-grid">
    <div class="summary-card critical">
      <div class="count">{{ severity_counts.critical }}</div>
      <div class="label">Critical</div>
    </div>
    <div class="summary-card high">
      <div class="count">{{ severity_counts.high }}</div>
      <div class="label">High</div>
    </div>
    <div class="summary-card medium">
      <div class="count">{{ severity_counts.medium }}</div>
      <div class="label">Medium</div>
    </div>
    <div class="summary-card low">
      <div class="count">{{ severity_counts.low }}</div>
      <div class="label">Low</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- === METHODOLOGY === -->
  <h2>Methodology</h2>
  <p>The assessment followed a structured 3-phase methodology:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Reconnaissance &amp; Mapping:</strong> An authenticated crawler enumerated all forms, input fields, and links across protected pages, producing a structured map of the application's attack surface.</li>
    <li><strong>Vulnerability Detection:</strong> Three independent detection modules tested each input for distinct vulnerability classes:
      <ul>
        <li><em>SQL Injection</em> — error-based payload injection across 8 payloads, response pattern matching against 15+ database error signatures</li>
        <li><em>Cross-Site Scripting</em> — reflective payload injection across 8 XSS variants, detection via unencoded payload reflection in responses</li>
        <li><em>Insecure Direct Object Reference</em> — sequential ID enumeration with MD5 content-hash comparison to detect unauthorized data access</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Reporting:</strong> Findings are aggregated and presented with proof-of-concept payloads, evidence, CVSS 3.1 base scores, and remediation guidance.</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- === TECHNICAL FINDINGS === -->
  <h2>Technical Findings</h2>

  {% for finding in findings %}
  <div class="finding {{ finding.severity | lower }}-finding">
    <div class="finding-header">
      <h3 class="finding-title">{{ loop.index }}. {{ finding.vulnerability }}</h3>
      <div>
        <span class="badge badge-{{ finding.severity | lower }}">{{ finding.severity }}</span>
        <span class="cvss">CVSS {{ finding.cvss_score }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="finding-meta">
      <div><strong>URL:</strong> {{ finding.url }}</div>
      <div><strong>Parameter:</strong> {{ finding.parameter }}</div>
      <div><strong>Method:</strong> {{ finding.method }}</div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">Proof of Concept</div>
    <pre>{{ finding.payload }}</pre>

    <div class="section-label">Evidence</div>
    <p>{{ finding.evidence }}</p>

    <div class="section-label">Impact</div>
    <p>{{ finding.impact }}</p>

    <div class="section-label">Remediation</div>
    <p>{{ finding.remediation }}</p>

    <div class="section-label">References</div>
    <ul>
      {% for ref in finding.references %}
      <li><a href="{{ ref.url }}" target="_blank">{{ ref.title }}</a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

  <!-- === CONCLUSION === -->
  <h2>Conclusion</h2>
  <p>
    The application contains {{ total_findings }} high-severity vulnerabilities that present significant
    security risk. Remediation should be prioritized based on the CVSS scoring and exploitability of each
    finding. All identified issues map to entries in the OWASP Top 10 (2021), which represents the most
    critical security risks to modern web applications.
  </p>
  <p>
    Following remediation, a retest is recommended to verify all vulnerabilities have been successfully
    addressed. Additionally, the development team should consider implementing the secure coding practices
    outlined in the OWASP Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS).
  </p>

  <!-- === FOOTER === -->
  <div class="footer">
    <p>Generated by Web Vulnerability Scanner v1.0 &mdash; {{ test_date }}</p>
    <p>Report prepared by {{ tester_name }} &middot; <a href="https://github.com/{{ github_user }}/web-vuln-scanner">github.com/{{ github_user }}/web-vuln-scanner</a></p>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>